      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "category-diverging",
      "description": "A text-labelled method category, not an interactive filter.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-category\">Diverging</span>",
      "css": ".ds-category{font-family:'Segoe UI',Inter,Arial,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.3;padding:5px 9px;border-radius:5px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;width:fit-content;color:#643a9e;background:#f0e9fb}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Agenda Method",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "activity-card",
      "description": "Progressive method disclosure on a flat working card.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-activity\"><details class=\"ds-disclosure\"><summary><div><h3 class=\"ds-title\">Brainstorming</h3><p class=\"ds-summary\">Generate a range of possible directions.</p></div><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></summary><p class=\"ds-detail\">Inspect the method steps and materials before your session.</p></details></article>",
      "css": ".ds-activity{font-family:'Segoe UI',Inter,Arial,sans-serif;border:1px solid var(--line,#dbe1ea);background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:20px 24px;color:var(--ink,#17243a)}.ds-disclosure>summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:20px;padding:4px 0;list-style:none;cursor:pointer}.ds-disclosure>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-disclosure>summary>svg{flex-shrink:0;transition:transform .18s}.ds-disclosure[open]>summary>svg{transform:rotate(180deg)}.ds-title{font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:650;line-height:1.35;margin:0}.ds-summary{font-size:.9375rem;color:var(--muted,#546277);margin:5px 0 0;line-height:1.5}.ds-detail{font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6;margin:18px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line,#dbe1ea);padding-top:16px;color:var(--muted,#546277)}.ds-disclosure>summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #789bff;outline-offset:3px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-disclosure>summary>svg{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Replacement Candidate",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "candidate-card",
      "description": "Compact alternative with an explicit replacement action.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-candidate\"><h3 class=\"ds-candidate-title\">Brainwriting</h3><p class=\"ds-candidate-meta\">20 min · 4–8 participants</p><button class=\"ds-replace\">Replace</button></article>",
      "css": ".ds-candidate{font-family:'Segoe UI',Inter,Arial,sans-serif;border:1px solid var(--line,#dbe1ea);padding:16px;border-radius:12px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#17243a)}.ds-candidate-title{font-size:1rem;font-weight:650;margin:0;line-height:1.35}.ds-candidate-meta{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted,#546277);margin:14px 0;line-height:1.5}.ds-replace{font-family:'Segoe UI',Inter,Arial,sans-serif;border:1px solid #bfc9d8;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#17243a);font-size:.875rem;font-weight:600;padding:7px 12px;min-height:36px;border-radius:8px;line-height:1.4;cursor:pointer;transition:background .16s,color .16s,border-color .16s}.ds-replace:hover{background:#edf1f7}.ds-replace:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #789bff;outline-offset:3px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-replace{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Constraint Notice",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "warning",
      "description": "A caution expressed in text as well as colour.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-warning\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m10.3 3.9-8 14a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3l-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4m0 4h.01\"/></svg><p class=\"ds-warning-copy\">This method exceeds the available time. Review the constraint before confirming.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-warning{font-family:'Segoe UI',Inter,Arial,sans-serif;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.5;display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--warning,#77510b);background:#fff6e2;border:1px solid #e8cd8b}.ds-warning>svg{flex-shrink:0}.ds-warning-copy{margin:0;line-height:1.5}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Workshop Desk",
    "overview": "Session Studio is a calm working surface for designers preparing a workshop. White surfaces, cool grey surroundings and ink typography support repeated inspection and editing. Blue identifies actions; restrained category tints help people scan an agenda without overwhelming its content.\n\nThe user's sketches establish a stacked agenda, progressively disclosed method and step guidance, and opposing intake and replacement panels. The simple double-diamond identity connects the workspace to the design process. This document consolidates the first build's provisional direction from its CSS and components; it does not record visual approval or a rendered accessibility audit.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Clear task hierarchy and restrained functional colour.",
      "Readable system sans with tabular minutes.",
      "Stacked agenda and nested native disclosures.",
      "Flat working surfaces; elevated dialogs only.",
      "No marketing sections or decorative imagery."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Labelled Colour Rule",
        "body": "Category and constraint colours always accompany text; colour alone never explains a method or warning.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stable Minutes Rule",
        "body": "Use tabular numerals for durations, elapsed-time labels, budget totals and catalogue ratings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Working Surface Rule",
        "body": "Use borders and tonal separation for ordinary content; reserve shadows for modal overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep method names, timing and the next action easy to scan.",
      "Do use tabular numerals for timing and labelled colour for categories and constraints.",
      "Do retain visible keyboard focus and native disclosure controls.",
      "Do preserve the opposing panels and stacked agenda established by the user's sketches.",
      "Do keep provenance and uncertain estimates visible in quiet supporting text."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce marketing sections or decorative imagery into the working app.",
      "Don't use colour alone to communicate a category, error or constraint.",
      "Don't add shadows to ordinary resting cards.",
      "Don't turn local introductory typography into a global display scale.",
      "Don't treat implementation gaps or unverified rendered behaviour as approved design rules."
    ]
  }
}
